      "resolution": "Only the natural/providential endowment in the contemporary passive être doué de is accepted. The fixed douer verb definition and doué past-participle frame are supported by Larousse’s explicit verbe passif and de-complement use. The infinitive and its IPA remain douer, without adopting doué pour, the absolute talented adjective or unrestricted modern active granting."
